drm/sprd: send the brightness again when the panel is enabled

The panel's init code resets its brightness, and a brightness write that
arrives while the panel is off fails with -ENXIO. Phosh writes the brightness
just before the panel finishes powering up on unblank, so the screen stayed
dark until the next brightness change (its idle-dim, 30 s later).
Re-send the last brightness once the panel is enabled, as the ESD recovery
path already does.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sprd/sprd_panel.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sprd/sprd_panel.c
@@ -487,6 +487,10 @@

 	panel->is_enabled = true;
 	mutex_unlock(&panel_lock);
+
+	if (panel->oled_bdev && panel->oled_bdev->props.brightness)
+		sprd_oled_set_brightness(panel->oled_bdev);
+
 	DRM_INFO("HS03 set init code exit\n");

 	return 0;
